trapped between the woods and a highway  in belarus  these people have been walking towards  the polish border anxious to enter the  european union  on the other side  polish security forces in riot gear part  of the 12 000 that have been stationed  there guarding the frontier  preventing hundreds of refugees and  migrants from breaching the border  but it is a deadlock that risks igniting  into another migration crisis on the  doorstep of the eu for months thousands  have been entering the block through  belarus at first via lithuania and  latvia now mainly through poland the eu  has accused belarusian leader alexander  lukashenko of orchestrating wave upon  wave of undocumented migrants and asylum  seekers in retaliation they say for  sanctions it imposed on his government  over its violent crackdowns on the  opposition  caught in the middle of this  brinkmanship those attempting to escape  the harsh conditions they find  themselves in with no shelter  being steered towards poland by  belarusian state border officials  some had taken the chance after hearing  that belarusian travel agents were  selling visa invitations to the eu  only to find themselves surviving for  weeks in the forest that border poland  and belarus  they give us the cutters they  they provide everything then but when  you say when you said to them okay i  want to go to mansec i want to go  i want to go back to my country it's so  dangerous they said no you should go to  boland bill belarus they bought the gun  to our to our heads  when we were when  when we said we need to go to mensa so  far poland's nationalist government has  refused help from the eu's frontier  agency despite reports by polish border  guards of hostile behaviour and threats  from belarusian forces and for those  stuck in this no man's land there is no  guarantee how long they will have to  face the elements with little access to  food and water  human pawns between two hostile  neighbors sonia gallego al jazeera
 

